{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unodorous-unvagrant-kite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py::test_push_loop_converges_under_contention`\n(added one commit ago by 4c4f, `f7aa0d5b5`) failed in CI on a change that provably\ncannot affect it, then the same test passed 18/18 locally on that same patch set.\n\nObserved once so far: GitHub Actions run **30665788197** (Gerrit change 1134, patch set 1,\n`gerrit-verify`), worker `popen-gw1`, ubuntu-latest, py3.13, git 2.54.0.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFailure output:\n\n```\nrc=1\ncompetitor pushes fired=1\nstdout:\nLocal tickets branch is ahead by 1 commit(s) — pushing.\nstderr:\nPush failed (non-retryable, exit 1): To .../origin.git\n ! [rejected]        HEAD -> tickets (fetch first)\n```\n\nThat message is emitted at `reconcile-bridge.yml:321`, the ELSE arm of the classifier at\n`:314`:\n\n```sh\nif echo \"$push_stderr\" | grep -qiE 'non-fast-forward|rejected|fetch first'; then\n```\n\nThe stderr shown contains BOTH `rejected` and `fetch first`, so the classifier should have\nmatched and taken the retry arm. It did not. On attempt 1 the competitor had already\npushed (`competitor pushes fired=1`), so this is the ordinary benign-contention path the\ntest exists to cover.\n\n## What has been ruled out\n\n- **Not caused by change 1134.** Its only in-loop edit is `:319`, inside the THEN arm —\n  unreachable in a run that took the ELSE arm. Its other edit (the pre-loop fetch)\n  demonstrably worked, since `:299` printed an ahead-count that requires `origin/tickets`\n  to have resolved.\n- **Not the classifier's pattern.** 20,000 iterations of the exact `grep -qiE` against the\n  exact stderr text from the failing run, under `set -euo pipefail`, produced 0\n  misclassifications — so a `pipefail`/SIGPIPE interaction on that pipeline is not\n  reproducible at this payload size.\n- **Not reproducible locally.** 18/18 passes on the failing patch set (10 serial, 8 under\n  parallel load), macOS, git 2.55.0.\n\n## Leads not yet tested\n\n- Whether `push_stderr` was actually EMPTY at classification time and the text in the\n  `:321` message came from a later expansion — i.e. `push_stderr=$(git push ... 2>&1)`\n  losing its capture under load. This is the leading hypothesis and is untested.\n- git 2.54.0 (CI) vs 2.55.0 (local) behavioural difference in what `git push` writes to\n  stderr vs stdout under `2>&1` capture.\n- CPU starvation on a loaded runner perturbing the competitor shim's 6-subprocess sequence.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThe test gates every change through `gerrit-verify`, so a flake here costs a full CI cycle\nper occurrence and trains reviewers to `recheck` reflexively. It also guards a real\nconvergence property (bug 4c4f), so weakening or skipping it is not the answer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The mechanism is reproduced deterministically (e.g. under enforced CPU contention or\n      git 2.54.0) rather than inferred.\n- [ ] Root cause named at a specific changeable artifact — the workflow's stderr capture,\n      the classifier, or the test harness's shim.\n- [ ] Fixed without weakening the convergence assertions the test exists to make.\n- [ ] File paths: `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`,\n      `tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py`.","id":"e161-596c-0b7e-42af","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","flaky-test"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_push_loop_converges_under_contention flakes in CI: push classified non-retryable on attempt 1"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785536291482849001,"uuid":"9046d833-6fdc-41b4-8fb6-553569cdee5a"}